{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:1b49e1665c6b1991","name":"Krayt Dragon Pearl","source":{"id":"source:reference-1b49e1665c6b1991","title":"Krayt Dragon Pearl","revision":20467,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:54:16Z","sha256":"2b72a44952578ddc10d4e81ca26c614ad3c3b3e84d03fecf0f97b32510e64756","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20467","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Krayt%20Dragon%20Pearl&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-1b49e1665c6b1991","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Color:"]}," Varies\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["DC Modifier:"]}," +10\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Krayt Dragon Pearls are found in the bellies of massive ",{"tag":"a","children":["Krayt Dragons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Krayt_Dragons?action=edit&redlink=1"}," that roam ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"},". Krayt Dragon Pearls come into being when existing gemstones deep in the desert sands of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"}," are consumed by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Krayt Dragon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Krayt_Dragon","referenceId":"reference:9e2806192a3a120a"},"; in the creature's belly, they are further compressed and refined until they reach a new level of clarity and beauty. Though obtaining one is usually a monumental task, a Krayt Dragon Pearl can be refined into a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber Crystal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber_Crystal"}," of great potency.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Obtaining a Krayt Dragon Pearl is no simple task, as many Jedi can attest. Krayt Dragon Pearls are so rare that finding even one on the open market would cost millions of credits, and such a jewel would be a fine centerpiece in any royal crown jewels. The few Jedi that have obtained Krayt Dragon Pearls over the years have done so by finding and slaying a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Krayt Dragon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Krayt_Dragon","referenceId":"reference:9e2806192a3a120a"},". However, ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Order"}," does not condone such an action, as hunting ",{"tag":"a","children":["Krayt Dragons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Krayt_Dragons?action=edit&redlink=1"}," is not only dangerous but also contributes to the extinction of the species.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["If you wield an attuned ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," with a Krayt Dragon Pearl, you gain a +3 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force"}," bonus on damage rolls.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
